<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/place.owl#"
     xml:base="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/place.owl"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:place="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/place.owl#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/place.owl">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To talk about places of things.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Place Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>Where is a certain thing located? What is located at this place?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl</cpannotationschema:extractedFrom>
        <cpannotationschema:hasAuthor>Aldo Gangemi</cpannotationschema:hasAuthor>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>We can represent, transitively, where something is located. It remains unspecified what kind of location relation we are trying to represent: reference location, partial location, physical location, social or metaphoric location, etc.
Moreover, temporal location is not caught with this pattern (you need a placement situation for that).</cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To talk about places of things.</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>The Colosseum is located in Rome.</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label moved to skos:prefLabel x3; label added x9; term declared x3;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Place Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.1 added rdfs:isDefinedBy for all named entities</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


